>>
Rule 1 (dimension of tensor must be at least 3)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 3
>>
Rule 2 (integer sections must divide the size of the third axis and be positive)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 3 ∧ v_2 > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 2) % v_2 = 0
>>
Rule 3 (indices list elements must be non-negative)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(int)} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 3 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[i] ≥ 0
>>
Rule 4 (indices tuple elements must be non-negative)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 3 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[i] ≥ 0
>>
Rule 5 (indices tensor must be 1D integer tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 3 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 1 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≥ 1 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 5
>>
Rule 11 (the third dimension of the input tensor must be positive)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 3 ∧ shape(v_1, 2) > 0
>>
Rule 12 (when indices_or_sections is an integer, it must be positive and less than or equal to the third dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 3 ∧ v_2 > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 2) ≥ v_2
>>
Rule 13 (when indices_or_sections is a list, the split indices must be sorted non-decreasingly)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(int)} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 3 ∧ (if v_2.len > 1 then ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 2] : v_2[i] ≤ v_2[i + 1])
>>
Rule 14 (when indices_or_sections is a tuple, the split indices must be sorted non-decreasingly)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 3 ∧ (if v_2.len > 1 then ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 2] : v_2[i] ≤ v_2[i + 1])
>>
Rule 15 (when indices_or_sections is a tensor, its elements must be 1D and bound between 0 and the split axis dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 3 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 1 ∧ min(v_2) ≥ 0 ∧ max(v_2) ≤ shape(v_1, 2)
>>
Rule 21 (split indices in list are within the bounds of the split dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(int)} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 3 ∧ (if v_2.len > 0 then ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[i] ≤ shape(v_1, 2))
>>
Rule 22 (split indices in tuple are within the bounds of the split dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 3 ∧ (if v_2.len > 0 then ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[i] ≤ shape(v_1, 2))
>>
Rule 23 (the number of split indices in the tensor cannot exceed the size of the split dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 3 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 1 ∧ shape(v_2, 0) ≤ shape(v_1, 2)
>>
Rule 24 (the first three dimensions of the input tensor must be positive)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 3 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 2) > 0
>>
Rule 25 (integer sections must be 1 or evenly divide the depth dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 3 ∧ (if v_2 > 1 then shape(v_1, 2) % v_2 = 0 else v_2 = 1)
